**Solution:** Added detectCurrentProject() call to onResume() so project is re-detected after returning from QR scanner","status":"open","priority":2,"issue_type":"bug","created_at":"2025-12-27T13:37:59.395962+05:30","updated_at":"2025-12-27T13:37:59.395962+05:30"}

{"description":"**RCA:** In AiimsLoginActivity.onCreate(), the authState Flow observer triggers navigateToMain() immediately when state is LOGGED_IN. Since user is already logged in when coming from AuthSettingsActivity Refresh Token button, this navigation happens before user can enter password.

**Fix:** Added isReauthMode class property (set from EXTRA_IS_REAUTH intent). Modified auth state observer to skip auto-navigation when isReauthMode=true, allowing user to enter password first.

**File:** AiimsLoginActivity.kt - Lines 40-41, 86, 114-117"}

{"description":"**RCA:** PinEntryActivity.refreshTokenButton click handler launched AiimsLoginActivity without passing EXTRA_IS_REAUTH and EXTRA_REAUTH_USERNAME flags, so login screen didn't recognize it was in re-auth mode.

**Fix:** Updated refreshTokenButton handler to: (1) Get current username from authManager.currentUser Flow, (2) Pass EXTRA_IS_REAUTH=true and EXTRA_REAUTH_USERNAME extras, (3) Use FLAG_ACTIVITY_NEW_TASK | FLAG_ACTIVITY_CLEAR_TASK for clean navigation.

**File:** PinEntryActivity.kt - Lines 276-293"}

{"description":"**RCA:** onBackPressed() checked for legacy 'is_reauth' intent flag instead of new 'isReauthMode' property. Also, launching with FLAG_ACTIVITY_CLEAR_TASK cleared the back stack so super.onBackPressed() minimized app.

**Fix:** Updated onBackPressed() to check isReauthMode property first. In re-auth mode, explicitly navigate to PinEntryActivity with NEW_TASK|CLEAR_TASK flags instead of calling super.onBackPressed().

**File:** AiimsLoginActivity.kt - Lines 278-292"}

